{
  "__inputs": [
    {
      "name": "DS_PROMETHEUS",
      "label": "Prometheus",
      "description": "",
      "type": "datasource",
      "pluginId": "prometheus",
      "pluginName": "Prometheus"
    }
  ],
  "__elements": {},
  "__requires": [
    {
      "type": "panel",
      "id": "gauge",
      "name": "Gauge",
      "version": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "grafana",
      "id": "grafana",
      "name": "Grafana",
      "version": "12.4.6"
    },
    {
      "type": "datasource",
      "id": "prometheus",
      "name": "Prometheus",
      "version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "type": "panel",
      "id": "stat",
      "name": "Stat",
      "version": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "panel",
      "id": "timeseries",
      "name": "Time series",
      "version": ""
    }
  ],
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "builtIn": 1,
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana",
          "uid": "-- Grafana --"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": true,
        "iconColor": "rgba(0, 211, 255, 1)",
        "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
        "type": "dashboard"
      },
      {
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "expr": "changes(process_start_time_seconds{job=\"jmx\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]) > 0",
        "hide": false,
        "iconColor": "blue",
        "name": "JVM restart",
        "textFormat": "{{instance}}",
        "titleFormat": "OpenNMS JVM restart"
      },
      {
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "expr": "changes(org_opennms_timeseries_ring_buffer_max_size_value{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]) > 0",
        "hide": false,
        "iconColor": "purple",
        "name": "Ring buffer resize",
        "textFormat": "{{instance}}",
        "titleFormat": "ring_buffer_size changed"
      }
    ]
  },
  "description": "Audience: network engineer. Entity-detail archetype: the timeseries persistence pipeline of one (or a few) OpenNMS instances — ring buffer saturation, sample throughput and loss, storage-plugin write latency, and the JVM context underneath. Sources: JMX Prometheus exporter on the OpenNMS JVM (onms_ts_* via jmx-exporter-timeseries.yml, jvm_* built-ins), scraped by Prometheus/VictoriaMetrics. Feeds the tuning decision: ring_buffer_size, writer_threads, WAL on/off, backend reachability.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "links": [
    {
      "asDropdown": true,
      "includeVars": true,
      "keepTime": true,
      "tags": [
        "opennms"
      ],
      "title": "OpenNMS dashboards",
      "type": "dashboards"
    }
  ],
  "panels": [
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 100,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Overiew",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Samples discarded because the ring buffer was full (onms_ts_samples_dropped_total), summed over the last 15 minutes per instance. Normal is exactly zero — every non-zero value is permanent data loss, matching the 'ring buffer is full' ERROR lines in collectd.log. Any red here: check ring buffer occupancy and write latency to the right, then raise org.opennms.timeseries.config.ring_buffer_size (power of two) or writer_threads in opennms.properties.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "percentChangeColorMode": "standard",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.4.6",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "label_replace(\n  sum by (instance) (increase(org_opennms_timeseries_ring_buffer_dropped_samples_count{instance=~\"$instance\"}[15m])),\n  \"node\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^:]+).*\")",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{node}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": "Dropped samples (errors) — last 15 min",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Samples queued in the ring buffer as a percentage of its configured capacity (onms_ts_ring_buffer_size / onms_ts_ring_buffer_max_size). Normal is near zero: collectd hands samples off and the writer drains them immediately. Amber at 70%, red at 90% — a buffer that sits high is one burst away from dropping. Sustained red means the storage plugin drains slower than collections arrive: look at write latency (right) and JVM health (below) before touching the buffer size.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 1,
          "mappings": [],
          "max": 100,
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 70
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 90
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "minVizHeight": 75,
        "minVizWidth": 75,
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showThresholdLabels": false,
        "showThresholdMarkers": true,
        "sizing": "auto"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.4.6",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "label_replace(\n  max by (instance) (org_opennms_timeseries_ring_buffer_size_value{instance=~\"$instance\"} / org_opennms_timeseries_ring_buffer_max_size_value{instance=~\"$instance\"} * 100),\n  \"node\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^:]+).*\")",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{node}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": "Ring buffer occupancy",
      "type": "gauge"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Rate of samples written through the timeseries integration layer (org_opennms_timeseries_samples_write_integration_count). This is the pipeline's delivered throughput; compare it against what collectd produces (collections/s × samples per collection) to see whether the writer keeps up. No threshold — the healthy value depends on the collection load, so read it together with occupancy and drops.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "fixedColor": "text",
            "mode": "fixed"
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "ops"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "percentChangeColorMode": "standard",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.4.6",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "label_replace(\n  sum by (instance) (rate(org_opennms_timeseries_samples_write_integration_count{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval])),\n  \"node\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^:]+).*\")",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{node}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": "Samples written per second",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "99th percentile of the storage-plugin write, amortized per sample (org_opennms_timeseries_samples_write_ts_99thpercentile, Dropwizard timer, milliseconds). This is the drain side of the ring buffer: when it rises, occupancy follows within seconds. Healthy baseline observed in this lab is ~25 ms; amber at 100 ms, red at 1 s. A p99 spike with a healthy backend usually means request-size or connection churn in the plugin, not VictoriaMetrics.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 100
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1000
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "ms"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 4,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "percentChangeColorMode": "standard",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.4.6",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "label_replace(\n  max by (instance) (org_opennms_timeseries_samples_write_ts_99thpercentile{instance=~\"$instance\"}),\n  \"node\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^:]+).*\")",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{node}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": "Storage write latency — p99",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "id": 101,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Persistence",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Queued samples as a percentage of capacity, per instance. The shape is the diagnosis: a flat line near zero is healthy; sawtooth means bursts the writer absorbs; a line pinned at 100% is the saturated state that produced nine hours of dropped samples on Aug 30–31. Threshold lines at 70/90% match the gauge above. Axis pinned 0–100 so instances compare.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisBorderShow": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
            "axisLabel": "",
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "barAlignment": 0,
            "barWidthFactor": 0.6,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 12,
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
            },
            "insertNulls": false,
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "showPoints": "never",
            "showValues": false,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            },
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "line"
            }
          },
          "decimals": 1,
          "mappings": [],
          "max": 100,
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 70
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 90
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "id": 5,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "last",
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "sortBy": "Max",
          "sortDesc": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "hideZeros": false,
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.4.6",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "label_replace(\n  max by (instance) (org_opennms_timeseries_ring_buffer_size_value{instance=~\"$instance\"} / org_opennms_timeseries_ring_buffer_max_size_value{instance=~\"$instance\"} * 100),\n  \"node\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^:]+).*\")",
          "legendFormat": "{{node}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": "Ring buffer occupancy over time",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Delivered throughput (written/s, blue) against loss (dropped/s, red) per instance. Written and dropped move together when the buffer saturates: the writer runs flat out while the overflow is discarded. Normal is dropped pinned at zero. Any red area is data permanently lost — correlate its start with the occupancy panel (left) and latency panel (right) to decide whether the buffer was too small (short burst) or the drain too slow (sustained).",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisBorderShow": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
            "axisLabel": "",
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "barAlignment": 0,
            "barWidthFactor": 0.6,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 15,
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
            },
            "insertNulls": false,
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "showPoints": "never",
            "showValues": false,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            },
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "off"
            }
          },
          "decimals": 1,
          "mappings": [],
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "ops"
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": ".*· written$"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "fixedColor": "#06A2BA",
                  "mode": "fixed"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": ".*· dropped$"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "fixedColor": "red",
                  "mode": "fixed"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "__systemRef": "hideSeriesFrom",
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byNames",
              "options": {
                "mode": "exclude",
                "names": [
                  "core-benchmark-01 · dropped"
                ],
                "prefix": "All except:",
                "readOnly": true
              }
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.hideFrom",
                "value": {
                  "legend": false,
                  "tooltip": true,
                  "viz": true
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 7
      },
      "id": 6,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "last",
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "sortBy": "Max",
          "sortDesc": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "hideZeros": false,
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.4.6",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "label_replace(\n  sum by (instance) (rate(org_opennms_timeseries_samples_write_integration_count{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval])),\n  \"node\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^:]+).*\")",
          "legendFormat": "{{node}} · written",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "label_replace(\n  sum by (instance) (rate(org_opennms_timeseries_ring_buffer_dropped_samples_count{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval])),\n  \"node\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^:]+).*\")",
          "legendFormat": "{{node}} · dropped",
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": "Samples written vs dropped (error rate)",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Percentiles of the storage-plugin write, amortized per sample (org_opennms_timeseries_samples_write_ts_*, Dropwizard timer, milliseconds). Percentiles, not the mean: a backend that answers fast except when it stalls has a mean that hides the stalls. p50 rising alone means everything got slower (backend or network); p99 diverging from p50 means intermittent stalls — connection resets, retries, GC pauses (check the JVM row below). The companion timer samples_write_integration_* times the in-memory hand-off into the integration layer (µs range) if you need to separate enqueue from drain. This is the leading indicator: latency moves first, occupancy second, drops third.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisBorderShow": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
            "axisLabel": "",
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "barAlignment": 0,
            "barWidthFactor": 0.6,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
            },
            "insertNulls": false,
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "showPoints": "never",
            "showValues": false,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            },
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "off"
            }
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "ms"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 7
      },
      "id": 7,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [
            "last",
            "max"
          ],
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "hideZeros": false,
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.4.6",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "label_replace(\n  max by (instance) (org_opennms_timeseries_samples_write_ts_50thpercentile{instance=~\"$instance\"}),\n  \"node\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^:]+).*\")",
          "legendFormat": "{{node}} · p50",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "label_replace(\n  max by (instance) (org_opennms_timeseries_samples_write_ts_95thpercentile{instance=~\"$instance\"}),\n  \"node\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^:]+).*\")",
          "legendFormat": "{{node}} · p95",
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "label_replace(\n  max by (instance) (org_opennms_timeseries_samples_write_ts_99thpercentile{instance=~\"$instance\"}),\n  \"node\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^:]+).*\")",
          "legendFormat": "{{node}} · p99",
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": "Storage write latency — p50, p95, p99",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "id": 102,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Java Virtual Machine",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Heap used against the configured maximum (jvm_memory_bytes_used / jvm_memory_bytes_max, area=heap). The ring buffer and the writer's in-flight batches live here: a heap running near its limit turns into long GC pauses, which stall the writer and show up as p99 latency spikes one panel up. Normal is a sawtooth well below the limit line. Used climbing toward the limit with no sawtooth is the leak signature.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisBorderShow": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
            "axisLabel": "",
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "barAlignment": 0,
            "barWidthFactor": 0.6,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
